  "notes": "Near-complete 0-100 per source (single source; verify with a native speaker). 62 source prints 'ਬਾਠ' (suspected typo); standard ਬਾਹਠ used. 99 'ਨੜੱਸੀ' is as printed in source; dialectal variants exist. Fractions are cognate with Hindi usage (dedh=1.5, dhai=2.5, savaa=1.25 e.g. ਸਵਾ ਸੌ = 125, paune=3/4 of next unit e.g. ਪੌਣੇ ਦੋ ਸੌ = 175, sadhe=+1/2 e.g. ਸਾਢੇ ਤਿੰਨ ਸੌ = 350). Punjabi is usually written in Gurmukhi in India and Shahmukhi in Pakistan; only Gurmukhi tables are included here."
